[2026-08-04 05:26:27] Felipe "Juca" Sanches: 📝 Blog — Part 127, "The keyboard that tells you its own version but won't hand over its ROM"

Committed 70e925f, registered in posts.json. The Cave of Wonders framing runs through it as a light structural device, not a costume:
- "The cave speaks its name" — the Version screen announcing PROGRAM : 941.
- "You may look, but you may not take" — the ROM test computes the sums and throws them away, showing only OK.
- "Touch nothing but the lamp" — no diagnostic hands over a byte; the update door only opens inward.
- "Two ways into the cave" — the diamond-in-the-rough gentle clip read vs. the forbidden-treasure code-exec route — closing on the real note that even the guardian at the door (the safeguard) cares how you phrase the request.
